WEBVTT

00:00.927 --> 00:07.599
As I stand in the wind on a hill by a port town,

00:00.927 --> 00:07.599
minatomachi oka no ue kaze wo uke

00:07.663 --> 00:14.690
mezurashii kurai atama wa karappo

00:07.663 --> 00:14.690
my head feels unusually empty.

00:15.275 --> 00:21.947
I was watching the town from the south side of the shore.

00:15.275 --> 00:21.947
haruka minami mukougishi de kono machi wo miteita

00:21.972 --> 00:28.186
And so I sunk my unsteady passion into the depths of the sea.

00:21.972 --> 00:28.186
guratsuita jounetsu wo umi ni shizumeta

00:29.080 --> 00:34.752
This surging power...

00:29.080 --> 00:34.752
tome donaku afureru chikara

00:29.080 --> 00:31.167
Black Jack

00:36.254 --> 00:42.509
It's something hidden in everyone, everywhere.

00:36.254 --> 00:42.509
sonnamono wa darenimo dokonimo hisonde iru mono

00:43.303 --> 00:48.265
Day after day, everyone tries their best.

00:43.303 --> 00:48.265
mainichi mainichi minna ganbaru

00:49.836 --> 00:57.191
But people get annoyed when I mention it.

00:49.836 --> 00:57.191
sore wo ieba hito wa mina kemutagaru

00:57.692 --> 00:59.383
Oh FREEDOM

00:59.383 --> 01:01.376
will be there

01:01.396 --> 01:04.356
It makes me glad...

01:01.396 --> 01:04.356
yokatta

01:04.601 --> 01:12.081
That I found my place here.

01:04.601 --> 01:12.081
ibasho ga koko ni attakara

01:12.134 --> 01:13.652
Oh WISDOM

01:13.652 --> 01:15.501
will be there

01:15.529 --> 01:18.170
I searched for the reason

01:15.529 --> 01:18.170
sagashita

01:18.171 --> 01:25.219
why we can believe in the same air

01:18.171 --> 01:25.219
onaji kuuki shinjirarerukoto

01:25.804 --> 01:32.684
as long as we're alive.

01:25.804 --> 01:32.684
ínochi aru kagiri

01:32.685 --> 01:34.770
He weaves the thread of life with his miraculous control of a scalpel.

01:34.854 --> 01:37.038
The genius surgeon who lives on a cape.

01:37.190 --> 01:39.801
His name is Black Jack.

02:00.107 --> 02:01.148
Doc!

02:01.441 --> 02:03.067
Doc!

02:03.110 --> 02:04.318
Oh, yes?

02:04.319 --> 02:06.696
These are all the bags you have, right?

02:07.906 --> 02:11.033
Also, would you mind taking the mail?

02:11.034 --> 02:12.375
I don't mind.

02:12.577 --> 02:13.536
It's no trouble.

02:13.537 --> 02:15.246
Doc!

02:15.247 --> 02:17.289
Look! Look!

02:17.290 --> 02:19.995
It's a souvenir for Sharaku!

02:20.836 --> 02:23.212
You can buy souvenirs on our way home.

02:23.213 --> 02:25.381
What kind of shell is this?

02:25.701 --> 02:27.341
It's a trumpet shell.

02:27.342 --> 02:28.277
Let's go.

02:28.760 --> 02:30.221
Aye-aye!

02:34.121 --> 02:37.221
Originally "The Blue Terror" by Tezuka Osamu.

02:34.121 --> 02:37.221
The Terror of the Azure Sea

02:45.861 --> 02:47.361
Taichi!

02:48.864 --> 02:50.114
How'd it go, Taichi?

02:50.907 --> 02:52.450
Perfect, Dad.

02:55.445 --> 02:56.662
See, Dad?

02:56.663 --> 02:59.248
You beat me.

02:59.407 --> 03:01.250
Let's head back.

03:02.002 --> 03:05.046
The Doctor's coming to visit us.

03:05.630 --> 03:08.055
The doctor? He's...

03:08.342 --> 03:09.050
Hmph!

03:12.095 --> 03:16.891
Hey Doc, do you also own the island we're visiting today?

03:17.077 --> 03:17.808
Yes, I do.

03:17.893 --> 03:19.226
It's called Sankai Island.

03:19.311 --> 03:22.855
What good does it do to buy so many islands?

03:23.315 --> 03:26.317
Islands teeming with life are beautiful, aren't they?

03:26.318 --> 03:28.861
I want to keep them that way.

03:30.572 --> 03:33.574
I won't let you waste any more money!

03:33.575 --> 03:35.951
Hey now. Don't call it a waste.

03:35.952 --> 03:38.120
But it is a waste!

03:38.121 --> 03:40.414
You'll understand one day.

03:47.707 --> 03:50.000
Hey!

03:50.626 --> 03:52.711
Huh? There are people.

03:52.894 --> 03:55.255
Hey, Doc!

03:55.457 --> 03:56.899
Hey! Taichi!

03:58.342 --> 03:59.676
What are you here for?!

03:59.982 --> 04:02.679
I brought food and other supplies.

04:02.983 --> 04:05.356
The regular guy could have done that.

04:05.683 --> 04:07.350
You didn't have to come.

04:07.351 --> 04:09.644
You don't appreciate our work?!

04:09.906 --> 04:12.023
We didn't ask for... Ouch!

04:12.273 --> 04:15.525
Hey, Taichi! He's the owner of this island!

04:16.235 --> 04:17.776
That's why I don't like him!

04:18.362 --> 04:21.573
Someone who lives in a city doesn't need to own an island!

04:21.574 --> 04:22.699
Stop it!

04:22.700 --> 04:23.658
But!

04:23.659 --> 04:28.038
Doc, did you buy these people with the island?

04:28.039 --> 04:29.309
What?!

04:31.084 --> 04:32.292
That's a good one!

04:32.293 --> 04:35.504
Pinoco, they both live here.

04:37.006 --> 04:38.131
We live by the sea.

04:38.132 --> 04:39.091
We're men of the sea!

04:45.014 --> 04:45.847
Wait!

04:45.848 --> 04:47.974
Wait up!

04:47.975 --> 04:51.770
Oh, I brought some mail for you too.

04:51.771 --> 04:53.188
Thanks a lot.

04:53.817 --> 04:56.358
It's not a pretty house, but come and relax for a while.

04:56.359 --> 04:59.194
Thanks. We want to stay the night if we can.

04:59.425 --> 05:02.572
We want to have the pleasure
of seeing the sun rise and set.

05:02.573 --> 05:05.617
City folk trying to act cool...

05:05.618 --> 05:06.618
Hey! Taichi!

05:09.247 --> 05:11.456
Is that it?

05:11.457 --> 05:12.624
Yes, it is.

05:15.753 --> 05:17.587
Have some tea.

05:17.778 --> 05:20.674
Tropical fruit too!

05:21.717 --> 05:24.594
Isn't it tough without any women around?

05:24.899 --> 05:28.390
It's been two years now since my wife
died, so I've gotten used to it.

05:28.596 --> 05:30.323
But I feel sorry for him,

05:31.102 --> 05:33.103
But he's growing up strong.

05:33.136 --> 05:35.439
No, he's still a kid.

05:35.887 --> 05:39.901
He tries to act strong, but he's
still not experienced enough.

05:40.199 --> 05:42.570
He's just a kid, he doesn't know what to fear.

05:43.239 --> 05:44.635
I'm not a kid!

05:45.170 --> 05:46.408
Yes, you are.

05:46.409 --> 05:47.739
Am not!

05:49.078 --> 05:51.705
You don't know the true terror of the sea yet.

05:51.706 --> 05:53.415
Terror of the sea?

05:53.416 --> 05:54.000
Hmph!

05:54.375 --> 05:55.959
I'm not scared of it at all!

05:56.335 --> 05:58.420
I'm different from those city folk there!

05:58.421 --> 05:59.614
What?!

05:59.922 --> 06:01.364
Want a piece of me?!

06:03.760 --> 06:05.056
Listen, Taichi.

06:05.303 --> 06:06.803
You may be the son of a fisherman,

06:07.430 --> 06:11.391
but you aren't a true fisherman yourself until
you know how truly terrifying the sea can be.

06:11.625 --> 06:13.685
I already know!

06:13.963 --> 06:16.730
No, you're still a kid.

06:16.731 --> 06:18.065
I don't get it!

06:18.066 --> 06:20.567
I don't understand what you're saying!

06:20.568 --> 06:21.763
I'm gonna go catch some fish.

06:23.295 --> 06:26.782
Don't forget to stay away from the western shore!

06:26.783 --> 06:27.674
I know!

06:29.196 --> 06:32.079
Hey Doc, I want to go see the sea too.

06:32.354 --> 06:33.538
That's fine.

06:33.539 --> 06:36.249
But you can't swim, so don't go in the water.

06:36.250 --> 06:37.042
OK!

06:37.710 --> 06:41.278
Also, don't go near the shore on the west side, OK?

06:41.547 --> 06:42.964
Is it that dangerous?

06:42.965 --> 06:44.049
Yes.

06:44.050 --> 06:46.468
That side is filled with sharp rocks.

06:46.780 --> 06:48.929
There are poisonous creatures too.

06:48.930 --> 06:50.931
Aye-aye!

06:56.312 --> 07:01.817
Doc, I'm thinking about sending Taichi
to the high school in town.

07:02.133 --> 07:05.570
I think this island's better for him than the town would be.

07:05.711 --> 07:08.049
Sure, the wind blows cold in town towards outsiders.

07:08.324 --> 07:12.369
But I want him to experience that harshness.

07:12.550 --> 07:13.975
Why's that?

07:17.834 --> 07:22.671
When he told me he wouldn't go to high school and
wanted to become a fisherman, I was overjoyed.

07:22.672 --> 07:24.923
But he takes the sea far too lightly.

07:24.924 --> 07:26.883
He may die there.

07:26.884 --> 07:30.011
We can't count on people helping
us if we stay on this island.

07:31.264 --> 07:34.345
I need him to mature a lot more.

07:34.809 --> 07:36.498
That's why you want to send him to town?

07:36.811 --> 07:40.397
But you'd be alone.

07:41.315 --> 07:44.499
I'm always alone at sea.

07:45.862 --> 07:49.619
This letter's a reply from the school.

07:49.991 --> 07:54.411
They said they'd give me the application
after meeting with me in person.

07:56.198 --> 07:59.332
I'm going to go see them now.

07:59.876 --> 08:00.616
Hey,

08:01.461 --> 08:04.004
then you can use the boat I used to get here.

08:04.263 --> 08:06.715
I'll be back by evening.

08:06.716 --> 08:09.651
Tell Taichi to get dinner ready when he returns.

08:11.804 --> 08:12.888
Yay!

08:24.942 --> 08:25.717
Hmm?

08:26.686 --> 08:27.152
Hey.

08:28.362 --> 08:29.488
I'm Pinoco.

08:29.489 --> 08:30.498
Nice to meet you.

08:31.817 --> 08:33.950
Hey now! You're rude!

08:34.764 --> 08:36.484
You're the ones that are rude!

08:36.517 --> 08:37.655
What are you talking about?

08:37.679 --> 08:39.940
Sankai Island is ours!

08:40.249 --> 08:42.501
We've lived here as far back as my granddad!

08:42.707 --> 08:45.718
I thought Doc bought this island.

08:46.214 --> 08:47.714
As if I care!

08:51.135 --> 08:52.630
A crab!

08:53.012 --> 08:54.513
Crab! Crab!

08:54.514 --> 08:55.472
Wait!

08:55.473 --> 08:56.972
Wait up!

08:58.309 --> 08:59.684
Ouch!

09:00.061 --> 09:01.645
Ow! Ow!

09:04.941 --> 09:06.784
Calm down!

09:08.111 --> 09:08.850
There.

09:10.613 --> 09:13.073
You need to grab crabs by their backs.

09:13.699 --> 09:15.559
City kids know nothing.

09:17.537 --> 09:20.455
You're smart.

09:20.987 --> 09:22.457
Anyone would know that.

09:23.626 --> 09:24.539
So,

09:25.231 --> 09:27.337
you catch fish with that stick?

09:27.338 --> 09:28.130
Yeah.

09:28.131 --> 09:30.924
But the northern shore wasn't good today.

09:30.925 --> 09:32.884
You can't catch any here?

09:32.885 --> 09:34.928
I want to catch fish.

09:34.929 --> 09:36.513
It's too hard for a kid.

09:36.514 --> 09:38.524
I'm not a kid!

09:38.850 --> 09:40.100
Then come with me.

09:41.060 --> 09:43.235
We'll move to the eastern shore.

09:44.814 --> 09:46.982
Hey, that's Doc's boat.

09:47.345 --> 09:48.525
Dad...

09:48.526 --> 09:49.985
Does he have something to do on the mainland?

09:50.128 --> 09:51.194
Fine!

09:51.195 --> 09:55.574
I'll get a big catch and surprise him!

09:55.575 --> 09:56.283
Let's go!

09:56.701 --> 09:58.410
Wait, Taichi!

09:58.411 --> 09:59.286
Wait up!

10:02.999 --> 10:04.958
It's so quiet...

10:07.670 --> 10:10.046
Why is it so quiet?

10:12.967 --> 10:13.967
I see!

10:14.552 --> 10:18.163
The tide's out now, so the sound
of the waves is further away.

10:27.106 --> 10:28.065
Strange...

10:28.407 --> 10:31.902
Neither the eastern nor southern shores have any fish.

10:34.280 --> 10:37.115
<i>Maybe the western shore...</i>

10:37.116 --> 10:39.117
Come on...

10:39.285 --> 10:40.577
Come on...

10:40.578 --> 10:42.037
Come...

10:42.038 --> 10:42.665
Oh?

10:42.955 --> 10:43.789
There!

10:43.831 --> 10:45.377
Here it comes!

10:55.301 --> 10:57.010
But it's a catch!

10:57.011 --> 10:58.345
Taichi!

10:58.763 --> 11:00.639
Taichi!

11:01.015 --> 11:04.851
Oh? Where'd he go?

11:18.825 --> 11:21.410
The low tide made this the perfect spot for fishing!

11:35.226 --> 11:37.551
The western shore's dangerous? Yeah, right!

11:37.969 --> 11:39.928
There's no better fishing spot than this!

11:48.229 --> 11:49.646
What?

12:09.959 --> 12:11.418
It's already this late.

12:12.670 --> 12:13.837
Pinoco?

12:14.881 --> 12:15.709
Taichi?

12:16.132 --> 12:17.549
Taichi!

12:17.675 --> 12:19.342
Taichi!

12:19.343 --> 12:21.136
Where'd he go?

12:21.137 --> 12:21.887
Pinoco?

12:22.513 --> 12:23.838
Doc!

12:24.652 --> 12:26.683
Just how late do you plan on playing?

12:26.684 --> 12:28.101
That's not it?

12:28.102 --> 12:32.147
I was catching fish with Taichi, but then he disappeared.

12:32.396 --> 12:36.109
I searched the eastern shore, and the southern
and northern ones too, but I couldn't find him.

12:36.389 --> 12:37.360
What about the western shore?

12:37.361 --> 12:40.113
But I'm not supposed-to go there, right?

12:40.656 --> 12:41.604
Could he...

12:42.283 --> 12:43.408
Dang...

12:45.787 --> 12:48.830
Dang it. It won't budge.

12:55.671 --> 12:56.547
Is that...

12:57.924 --> 12:58.840
That's Taichi.

12:58.841 --> 12:59.852
Taichi!

13:02.637 --> 13:04.312
Taichi, what's this?

13:04.395 --> 13:05.199
It's a giant clam.

13:05.309 --> 13:06.723
It got my leg.

13:07.194 --> 13:08.725
It's huge.

13:08.951 --> 13:12.907
It's buried between the rocks and
the sand, and it won't budge.

13:13.106 --> 13:15.257
This isn't something just anyone can do.

13:15.835 --> 13:18.151
We'll have to wait for your dad to come back.

13:18.411 --> 13:21.154
But the tide's already starting to rise.

13:21.155 --> 13:22.153
What?

13:22.448 --> 13:24.469
How long do we have before it comes in?

13:24.867 --> 13:26.006
I don't know.

13:26.327 --> 13:27.613
Two hours, maybe?

13:28.273 --> 13:30.807
It becomes twice as deep as my height.

13:31.207 --> 13:33.987
You'll drown for sure like this.

13:34.526 --> 13:37.254
Taichi, where do you keep the
scuba gear and oxygen tank?

13:37.451 --> 13:38.663
In the storage shack.

13:38.923 --> 13:39.756
Doc!

13:40.508 --> 13:41.523
Wait here.

13:41.717 --> 13:42.717
Let's go, Pinoco!

13:42.757 --> 13:44.966
Doctor...

13:45.889 --> 13:47.929
Don't worry, we'll save you.

13:54.981 --> 13:55.731
Is this it?

13:56.607 --> 13:58.567
Darn. It's padlocked.

13:59.402 --> 14:03.363
Pinoco, go ask Taichi where the
key for the storage shack is.

14:03.364 --> 14:05.449
You mean I have to go back?

14:05.450 --> 14:06.032
Hurry!

14:06.148 --> 14:07.200
Aye-aye!

14:07.702 --> 14:08.677
Damn...

14:30.141 --> 14:32.768
Doc, he doesn't know.

14:32.769 --> 14:34.603
He said it'd probably be somewhere in the house.

14:34.979 --> 14:37.230
We can't open it without the key.

14:37.231 --> 14:38.648
Pinoco, we must find it!

14:38.649 --> 14:39.176
OK!

14:39.400 --> 14:41.401
Key! Key! Key!

14:41.492 --> 14:43.278
Key! Key!

14:43.279 --> 14:45.197
Where's the key?

14:47.492 --> 14:48.951
Damn, where is it?

14:49.149 --> 14:51.229
Book: Sea Creatures

14:51.704 --> 14:54.242
Doc, I can't find it.

14:57.960 --> 15:01.088
Pinoco, keep searching for the key.

15:01.089 --> 15:02.130
What about you?

15:02.757 --> 15:03.579
It's time for an operation.

15:04.092 --> 15:07.155
But I've never performed an operation like this before.

15:14.644 --> 15:15.309
D...

15:15.895 --> 15:16.762
Dad...

15:17.021 --> 15:17.935
Taichi!

15:19.565 --> 15:20.464
Doc!

15:21.401 --> 15:23.340
Did you find the key?

15:27.291 --> 15:28.463
What's that?

15:28.825 --> 15:30.964
You want to break the shell with a hammer?

15:31.285 --> 15:33.036
That'll crush my leg!

15:33.037 --> 15:33.537
No.

15:33.788 --> 15:34.753
It's a wedge.

15:38.113 --> 15:38.667
All right.

15:39.085 --> 15:41.928
I can't pull out my leg with that.

15:42.130 --> 15:43.417
But I need to stick my arm in.

15:43.714 --> 15:44.357
Your arm?

15:45.550 --> 15:47.092
This is your encyclopedia.

15:48.261 --> 15:53.098
It says that clams have two adductor muscles
and those are used to keep the shell shut.

15:53.432 --> 15:55.349
I'll force the shell open with my scalpel.

15:55.726 --> 15:58.812
If l can sever the adductor muscles,
it should open the shell.

15:59.480 --> 16:02.260
And if I can figure out where they are, I should
be able to do it without seeing them.

16:03.359 --> 16:05.360
What if that doesn't work?

16:05.945 --> 16:08.353
Then you might as well give up.

16:08.698 --> 16:12.619
If something goes wrong, my arm will
get stuck and then I'll die too.

16:18.082 --> 16:18.790
Let's do it.

16:21.919 --> 16:23.385
<i>First, the mantle.</i>

16:33.806 --> 16:35.056
Are you all right, Taichi?

16:35.327 --> 16:38.480
The clam feels the pain too.

16:39.687 --> 16:42.163
<i>The tide's rising quicker than I thought it would.</i>

16:54.018 --> 16:55.775
D-Doc...

17:04.045 --> 17:05.530
Doc?

17:13.970 --> 17:15.514
I'm going to die!

17:15.818 --> 17:16.598
Come on!

17:16.682 --> 17:17.474
Don't give up!

17:17.975 --> 17:19.559
I'm going to die!

17:19.685 --> 17:21.450
I'm going to drown to death!

17:23.272 --> 17:25.273
I'm going to die!

17:25.274 --> 17:26.212
Taichi!

17:27.193 --> 17:29.444
Taichi, are you really the son of a fisherman?

17:29.732 --> 17:33.949
Or are all men of the sea wusses like you?

17:35.952 --> 17:38.260
Don't mock men of the sea!

17:39.080 --> 17:40.789
I haven't given up yet!

17:40.790 --> 17:41.680
Believe in me!

17:52.760 --> 17:53.802
Is this...

17:54.262 --> 17:55.304
Here it is.

17:55.763 --> 17:56.611
This is it.

17:59.642 --> 18:01.033
Doc?

18:01.394 --> 18:03.147
I've severed one.

18:03.438 --> 18:04.771
One more to go.

18:04.901 --> 18:05.689
Doc...

18:05.690 --> 18:07.300
This'll be it.

18:07.525 --> 18:08.175
Let's go!

18:15.950 --> 18:16.763
Damn...

18:36.116 --> 18:37.512
I was...

18:37.513 --> 18:39.804
<i>I was a fool, Dad.</i>

18:40.808 --> 18:43.070
<i>The sea's the same as it always is, but...</i>

19:00.445 --> 19:02.688
<i>Damn. That's the best I can...</i>

19:05.124 --> 19:07.744
<i>Don't die, Taichi!</i>

19:22.850 --> 19:24.737
Doc!

19:25.603 --> 19:27.944
Doc!

19:28.189 --> 19:30.578
Taichi!

19:30.983 --> 19:33.819
Doc!

19:40.201 --> 19:42.661
Doc!

19:42.995 --> 19:44.621
Doc!

19:44.622 --> 19:45.664
How's Taichi?

19:45.665 --> 19:47.332
Is he dead?

19:47.633 --> 19:48.576
Are you kidding?

19:48.876 --> 19:51.623
A man of the sea won't die so easily.

19:52.356 --> 19:53.755
Yay!

19:53.756 --> 19:55.537
You've done it!

19:58.761 --> 20:02.013
Hey, Taichi, are you awake?

20:02.807 --> 20:03.836
Dad.

20:04.058 --> 20:06.017
How do you feel?

20:06.686 --> 20:08.638
O-OK,

20:09.272 --> 20:10.612
I was scared.

20:10.940 --> 20:12.190
I thought I was going to die.

20:13.067 --> 20:15.277
I really thought I was going to die.

20:15.278 --> 20:16.319
Are you...

20:16.320 --> 20:19.593
Do you hate the sea now?

20:24.704 --> 20:25.493
No.

20:26.456 --> 20:27.945
The sea's scary,

20:28.332 --> 20:29.209
but...

20:30.835 --> 20:33.420
I still love the sea.

20:34.839 --> 20:36.065
Taichi!

20:50.313 --> 20:53.302
It's really pretty!

20:53.672 --> 20:56.032
Seikai High School
Admissions Guidelines

20:58.071 --> 20:59.332
Hey, isn't that...

21:00.948 --> 21:03.138
He doesn't need it anymore.

21:15.963 --> 21:17.547
Bye-bye!

21:17.757 --> 21:20.342
Bye-bye!

21:23.096 --> 21:26.370
Hey, Doc, look.

21:27.218 --> 21:28.996
Hey, Doctor!

21:29.227 --> 21:33.701
I'll feed you delicious clams when
you come back next time!

21:34.023 --> 21:36.666
Come again!

21:37.568 --> 21:38.432
Hey Taichi,

21:38.653 --> 21:40.695
I'm going to go out to fish now,

21:40.696 --> 21:43.657
but you don't have to come along.

21:44.158 --> 21:45.867
Wait, Dad.

21:45.868 --> 21:47.532
I can...

21:48.454 --> 21:49.893
I can come with you.

21:50.998 --> 21:53.557
You never know what might happen at sea.

21:54.416 --> 21:55.897
You think you know everything now?

21:56.129 --> 22:02.342
Hey Doc, let's work harder and harder, and then
we can buy all the islands in the world.

22:02.343 --> 22:04.344
Hey now. Don't ask for the impossible.

22:04.345 --> 22:06.007
It's not impossible.

22:10.527 --> 22:17.533
I want to capture your heart with my silly smile.

22:10.527 --> 22:17.533
itazura no hohemi de muchuu ni sasetaino

22:17.534 --> 22:24.706
Only look straight at me.

22:17.534 --> 22:24.706
massugu na kimi no me ni watashi wo utsushitene

22:24.751 --> 22:32.008
Being kind isn't good enough.

22:24.751 --> 22:32.008
yasashii dake dewa nanika tarinaino

22:32.009 --> 22:42.518
I want to get in touch with your true heart, deep
within the you that nobody else sees.

22:32.009 --> 22:42.518
dare nimo misenai kokoro no oku no sotto furetai

22:42.519 --> 22:47.899
Being in the gentle sunlight,

22:42.519 --> 22:47.899
yawaraka na hizashi abite

22:47.900 --> 22:57.283
I wish on the clover that plays the melody of dreams,

22:47.900 --> 22:53.105
yume wo kanaderu clover

22:53.560 --> 22:57.284
kaze ni negai wo nosete

22:57.284 --> 23:08.044
and I search for a ray of hope beyond the blue skies,

22:57.284 --> 23:08.044
aoi sora no mukou e kibou no hikari sagasuno

23:08.045 --> 23:13.132
because I want to stay by your side forever.

23:08.045 --> 23:13.132
zutto soba ni itakara

23:13.133 --> 23:26.103
The promise we made long ago in a far away place...

23:13.133 --> 23:26.103
haruka kanata de zutto mae kara

23:26.104 --> 23:33.027
is finally coming to a realization, overcoming the incredible distance,

23:26.104 --> 23:33.027
hikari ni terasare michibikareru youni

23:33.028 --> 23:43.913
just as it was lead by the light.

23:33.028 --> 23:36.961
sora no hate tooku

23:37.054 --> 23:43.854
toki wo koete ima tadori tsuku

23:45.107 --> 24:15.097
An Invader from the Sky

23:46.739 --> 23:48.094
Sharaku!

23:48.327 --> 23:49.487
Show me!

23:49.513 --> 23:52.706
They might want to use me as an
experiment for research.

23:52.840 --> 23:54.647
It's only for an examination.

23:55.983 --> 23:57.627
I knew it. My mom is...

23:58.970 --> 24:00.873
You must be the invader's boss!

24:01.007 --> 24:02.320
Let's escape!

24:04.334 --> 24:06.501
That man in black's an invader!

24:06.634 --> 24:09.613
If it's hopeless, it's best to
just tell him that!

24:09.720 --> 24:10.973
It's true.

24:11.850 --> 24:14.317
Next Karte - An Invader from the Sky.

24:16.059 --> 24:17.663
Karte NG...

24:18.978 --> 24:20.687
How late do you plan on play...

24:20.688 --> 24:21.522
An octopus?
